From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Poyu Chen <me@poyu.xyz>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 06:01:45 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] pwm: omap-dmtimer: defer probe until the timer device exists

The timer can sit under a ti-sysc target module whose child devices are
created after the PWM driver first probes (timer 9 on OMAP4). Return
-EPROBE_DEFER instead of failing for good.

Upstream: not submitted
---
 drivers/pwm/pwm-omap-dmtimer.c | 6 ++++--
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/pwm/pwm-omap-dmtimer.c b/drivers/pwm/pwm-omap-dmtimer.c
index 1858a7740..01087f125 100644
--- a/drivers/pwm/pwm-omap-dmtimer.c
+++ b/drivers/pwm/pwm-omap-dmtimer.c
@@ -322,8 +322,10 @@ static int pwm_omap_dmtimer_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 
 	timer_pdev = of_find_device_by_node(timer);
 	if (!timer_pdev) {
-		dev_err(&pdev->dev, "Unable to find Timer pdev\n");
-		ret = -ENODEV;
+		/* The timer can sit under a ti-sysc target module whose
+		 * children are created after this driver first probes. */
+		dev_dbg(&pdev->dev, "Timer pdev not yet available, deferring\n");
+		ret = -EPROBE_DEFER;
 		goto err_find_timer_pdev;
 	}
 
